<template><section class="card trust-policy"><h2>Collection boundaries</h2><p>Capture is visible and governed by your company’s policy. Employees can review their own retained captures and delete their screenshots without score penalties.</p><details><summary>What this platform does not collect as separate records</summary><ul><li>No keystroke-content log or clipboard scraping.</li><li>No mouse-coordinate or click-history log. Last-input timestamps support idle detection; optional timing review uses aggregate intervals.</li><li>No file-system scan or automatic upload of personal documents.</li><li>No webcam or microphone recording.</li><li>No extraction of passwords from browsers or password managers.</li><li>No dedicated government-ID or payroll fields.</li><li>No inventory of background processes; activity samples identify the foreground application and window.</li></ul></details><p class="notice"><strong>Screen content matters.</strong> Screenshots, optional silent video, window titles and optional URLs can contain personal or sensitive information, including visible credentials or document text. Automated redaction and sensitive-app exclusions are not implemented. Avoid displaying sensitive content while capture is active; sign out or quit the agent to stop it.</p><p>The platform also stores account and device details, login/activity timestamps, audit logs and employee-entered HR information. It processes sign-in credentials; account passwords are hashed, and the agent does not save the login password.</p><a href="/api/admin/trust-guide">Download trust &amp; deployment facts</a><p class="small muted">This describes implemented behavior, not legal advice or a compliance certification. Hosting, backups, FTPS and email delivery are controlled by your organization.</p></section></template>
